---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SkillsTicker from '../components/SkillsTicker.astro';
const experience = [
  [
    'May 2022 – Nov 2024',
    'Research assistant · Universitas Syiah Kuala',
    'Worked with Prof. Dr. Ir. Roslidar on thermal-image classification, including CNN feature extraction and XGBoost. Co-authored research presented at IEEE CENIM 2024.',
  ],
  [
    'Feb – Jul 2022',
    'Machine learning cohort · Bangkit',
    'Led machine learning for the BADI team prototype, collaborating with Android and Cloud Computing teammates.',
  ],
  [
    'Jul – Aug 2022',
    'Intern · Telkom Indonesia',
    'Worked with network operations at IOC Plasa Telkom Aceh.',
  ],
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  activeNav="about"
  description="Muhammad Hafiz’s engineering background, research journey, and current interests."
>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="page-head about-intro">
      <h1 class="typing-heading">
        <span class="sr-only">Hi, I'm Muhammad Hafiz.</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true" data-typewriter>
          Hi, I'm Muhammad Hafiz.
        </span>
      </h1>
    </header>
    <section class="about-profile">
      <div>
        <p>
          I studied Computer Engineering at Universitas Syiah Kuala and worked
          on machine learning research in thermal imaging. That experience made
          me care about the whole path from a question to an evaluated result.
        </p>
        <p>
          Today, I build reproducible analytical systems and explore how
          software can make their evidence easier to inspect. Football analytics
          gives that work a concrete setting: profiles and rankings must remain
          understandable alongside what the data cannot tell us.
        </p>
        <p>
          Currently exploring: ML Systems, AI / LLM Engineering, Football
          Analytics, and research-driven products.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <SkillsTicker />
    <section class="prose">
      <h2>Research journey</h2>
      <p>
        At Universitas Syiah Kuala, I worked with Prof. Dr. Ir. Roslidar,
        Khairun Saddami, and Essy Harnelly on Breast Thermal Image
        Classification. The study compares VGG16 and ResNet50 features with
        XGBoost for a three-class DMR task. Its IEEE CENIM 2024 publication is
        part of my research background.
      </p>
      <p>
        The{' '}
        <a href="/work/breast-thermal-classification/">research case study</a>{' '}
        preserves the reported method and labels a source discrepancy in the
        validation results.
      </p>
      <h2>Experience</h2>
      <div class="timeline-list">
        {experience.map(([period, title, copy]) => (
          <div class="timeline-row">
            <span class="period">{period}</span>
            <div>
              <h3>{title}</h3>
              <p>{copy}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <h2>Education</h2>
      <div class="timeline-row">
        <span class="period">Aug 2019 – Nov 2024</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Bachelor of Computer Engineering</h3>
          <p>Universitas Syiah Kuala</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>
        Exchange coursework included Ethical Hacking at AMIKOM (4.00), Mobile
        Computing and Data Mining at Dian Nuswantoro (3.79), Digital Image
        Processing at UGM (3.25), and Information Security at Universitas
        Indonesia (3.00).
      </p>
      <h2>Credentials</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>TensorFlow Developer certification, 2022</li>
        <li>Bangkit graduate, Machine Learning path, 2022</li>
        <li>Machine Learning specialization coursework on Coursera, 2022</li>
        <li>Co-authored IEEE CENIM 2024 publication</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="project-links">
        <a href="/work/">Explore my work →</a>
        <a href="/resume/">Resume →</a>
        <a href="/contact/">Get in touch →</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
